WEBVTT

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:08.190
Stepping out on
an ordinary Sunday

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:14.690
Stepping out!
A miracle's gonna happen

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.530
It's my day!

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:27.100
Maybe I'll throw off my pajamas

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:34.510
and head out to see her right now

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.890
I always turned my eyes away,
thinking she'd hate me

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:49.290
Now I'm saying goodbye
to that negative attitude

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:55.070
My favorite shoes
will always take me

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:02.210
To a place where I'll be happy

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:09.710
It's not someone else
I want to embrace

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:15.850
But a version of
myself that's not fake

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.920
I just want to walk

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.460
Not on tip-toe

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:26.430
Not downcast, either

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:35.340
Just I'm stepping out
on an ordinary Sunday

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:41.780
Stepping out!
Making a little try, try, try

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.050
It's my day!

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:03.020
<i>My first morning
living on my own.</i>

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.770
<i>Today, I begin my new life.</i>

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.520
<i>Why'd you go and tell
Nishikado and Mimasaka?</i>

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.520
<i>I was so embarrassed.</i>

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.860
<i>Why not? It was the truth.</i>

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.090
<i>It may be the truth,
but some things shouldn't be told.</i>

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:33.260
<i>You like to stuff everything
inside of you like that, huh?</i>

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.940
<i>Why don't you just be honest, for once?</i>

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.440
<i>Good-bye to sad yesterdays...</i>

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:44.710
Oh, no!

00:02:53.050 --> 00:03:01.930
"Hurricane Approaching!!"

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.870
Say, Tsukushi...
How do you like living alone?

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.970
It's the best!
I made French toast this morning.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.140
Wow!

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:18.910
Of course, I burnt it a little.

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.130
A little?

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.650
You got me.
Actually, I turned it into charcoal.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.050
I figured.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.490
That's so like you.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.530
Tsukushi?

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:18.740
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:20.780
What's wrong?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:21.980
It's nothing.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:25.080
There's someplace I want to go.
Go on ahead, will you?

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:26.340
Okay.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:38.020
<i>I just can't let go...</i>

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.450
<i>Something precious is standing
right before you.</i>

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.780
<i>You can just reach out
and grasp it...</i>

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:44.160
<i>But you don't even try. How can you
possibly understand how I feel?</i>

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:01.810
<i>I wonder if Rui Hanazawa
is mad at me.</i>

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:08.950
<i>But maybe it's best that
I don't see him now.</i>

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:12.720
<i>Shigeru...</i>

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:17.160
<i>I guess she won't come
to see me anymore.</i>

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.630
<i>Not after I caught her
in the act.</i>

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.680
Stupid! Stupid! I'm so stupid!

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:52.790
Oh, that's the ultra-elite
girls' school, isn't it?

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:54.300
Right!

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:58.200
They said I should bring
my friends over.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:01.630
Whoa! All the girls we
 can choose from, right?

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:02.570
Oh, yeah.

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:03.970
Huh?

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:05.970
We have no choice but to go.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.510
Go? Where?

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:12.280
Weren't you listening?
You know, that new nightclub?

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.150
New club?

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:17.770
<i>Shot Site.</i>
We're gonna party with all those rich girls.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:18.450
A party!

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:22.320
Not interested...

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:23.920
Come on...

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:25.450
You're coming, aren't you, Rui?

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:26.360
Nope.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.830
Why do you have such long faces?

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.140
You're putting the F4 to shame.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.120
Hey, Tsukasa!

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:06.100
What are you asking <i>me</i> for?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:14.540
Well, those two got weird after going
to that monkey's villa with you.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.610
Something must have happened, right?

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.780
<i>How can you possibly
understand how I feel?</i>

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.510
I don't know.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:31.590
If they're acting weird,
it's got nothing to do with me!

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:41.130
<i>My scars keep getting deeper...</i>

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:56.380
<i>I managed not to run into
 Domyoji or Shigeru, today.</i>

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:59.250
Hey, Tsukushi.
How about going for some tea?

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:02.150
I'm sorry. I have to work today.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:04.420
I see. Maybe next time.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:06.320
Oh, that's right!

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:08.160
What is it, Tsukushi?

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.900
Since I'm living alone now,
let's get together at my place sometime.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.670
Oh, really?

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:16.230
Yeah!

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:24.830
But not for a while, I guess.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.480
I haven't straightened up
the place yet.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:30.050
I've got some
redecorating to do.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:32.420
Redecorating? That sounds fun.

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:35.410
Let me know and I'll help you.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:36.350
Okay.

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:41.960
<i>Domyoji...</i>

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:47.440
Makino.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.470
I'll see you tomorrow, Tsukushi.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.210
Makino. I have to talk to you.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.310
There's nothing I want
to hear from you.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.210
Shut up and listen to me.

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:03.350
No.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:04.850
Out of my way.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.400
<i>The warmth of his hand...</i>

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.550
<i>His arm... isn't mine!</i>

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:13.720
Makino!

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:27.970
<i>That arm belongs to...
It belongs to Shigeru, now.</i>

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:50.790
Sengoku-ya

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:58.900
<i>His arm... isn't mine!</i>

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.000
Thank you very much.

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:08.610
Shall we close up?

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.810
Tsukushi! What are you doing?

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:14.810
What is it?

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:16.510
Come on...

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:18.680
Oh!

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:23.240
Tsukushi...
It's been hard, hasn't it?

00:12:23.240 --> 00:12:24.890
What are you talking about?

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.230
It must be lonely, living by yourself.

00:12:29.460 --> 00:12:33.500
It's not really...
No, maybe you're right.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.570
I'll get used to it.
Don't worry.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:42.410
Tsukushi the weed can thrive
in any environment.

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:48.210
<i>Tsukushi...</i>

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:12.500
I LOVE YOU

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.200
<i>My head is spinning...</i>

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:52.240
<i>There are so many things
my heart has to sort out.</i>

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:56.180
<i>I have no idea where to begin.</i>

00:13:58.550 --> 00:13:59.850
<i>Rui Hanazawa?</i>

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:15.990
Why did you stop?

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.500
Oh, you're here?

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:23.330
You haven't played the violin
in a long time.

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:27.110
I didn't feel like playing.

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:33.310
But I shouldn't have done it.
I can't play like before.

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:36.810
That's not true. It was wonderful.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:42.690
I can't hear
the violin's voice anymore.

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:45.460
The violin's voice?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.420
Yeah...

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:51.600
Is it because of Shizuka?

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:52.860
No...

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:55.930
I'm the one who ran away.

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.200
<i>Rui Hanazawa...</i>

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.930
<i>I'm the one who ran away...</i>

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:03.700
<i>But not me. I'm not running...</i>

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.050
Y-yes?

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:19.680
Tsukushi!

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:21.070
Kazuya?

00:17:21.070 --> 00:17:23.020
Yuki and Maki came, too.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:26.090
Your redecorating crew is here.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:28.290
Here we come!

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.130
You guys...

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:38.070
What do you think?

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.560
Looks good.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.560
I'm getting good at it.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:44.190
Take a look at this, will you?

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:44.740
Where?

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:46.640
Wow!

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:50.620
A different color
really makes a difference.

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:55.770
Instead of living alone,
you should come and live with us.

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:57.060
We've got room to spare.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:02.160
Thanks. But I don't know
when my family might come back.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:06.360
Besides, I've never had a place
to call my own.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:13.440
And, thanks to your help,
this has turned into a great apartment.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:15.440
Isn't it great to have
such good friends?

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:17.810
I'm very grateful.

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:23.680
Does Tsukasa know
you're living alone now?

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:25.750
No, he doesn't.

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:29.620
There no reason to tell him.
He's nothing to me.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:31.020
That's right!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.770
He's got nothing to do
with our world.

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:38.460
Okay, now I'll repaper
the doors!

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:41.830
I'm back!
I picked up some riceballs.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.130
Hurray! I'm hungry.

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:46.400
- Let's eat.
- I'll heat some water.

00:18:47.970 --> 00:18:48.920
Here's the tea.

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:49.840
Thanks.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:56.480
<i>I'm lucky to have friends.</i>

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:07.190
Tsukushi. Don't you think
this furniture is cute?

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:09.630
Oh, yes! It's adorable!

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:11.300
This one's nice, too.

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:12.960
Let me see.

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:16.800
What?! 50,000 yen?
I could never afford it.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:19.950
I guess not. That would be
your whole paycheck.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:20.930
I see...

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.310
Yes. I've got to scrimp and save.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:27.340
Quit yakking and help me,
will you?

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.810
Oh, I'm sorry...

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:31.020
Did you finish the other door?

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:31.820
Yeah.

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:36.170
Kazuya, you're good
at papering doors.

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:37.320
You think so?

00:19:38.020 --> 00:19:39.690
Why don't you
get a job doing this?

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:41.290
Oh, come on!

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:43.700
It's great to have a craft.

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:47.530
Maybe I will...

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:53.300
<i>I'd better stop thinking
about Domyoji and Shigeru...</i>

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:59.580
<i>At least while I'm surrounded
by such good friends.</i>

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.450
What's going on?

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:15.530
That place was deserted
all this time.

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:21.070
Wow...
They're using five bulldozers!

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.920
<i>Oh... What's happening here?</i>

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:47.930
Tsukushi...

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:52.070
Kazuya... What are they doing?

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:56.430
A transfer student's parents
are donating a new facility.

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:59.040
That's why they're clearing
the place.

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:01.510
A new facility?

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:04.310
Yes. The Okawahara Memorial Hall.

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:09.980
S-Shigeru?!

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:16.920
That uniform...

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:22.790
N-no way...

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:26.300
I transferred here.
Good to see you.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.100
<i>No way!</i>

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:30.230
<i>I must be dreaming!</i>

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:42.710
<i>Yes. It's got to be a nightmare.</i>

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:05.580
Will I ever make it that far?

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:10.330
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:22:12.150 --> 00:22:19.800
Some day, the whole world

00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:25.610
will have its eyes on me.

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:33.360
Yeah, after our graduation ceremony

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:38.980
we all wrote our dreams on the wall.

00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:45.600
A lot of time has passed since then

00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:52.000
but I'm just the same as I was on that day!

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:58.900
Keep trying your best! 
Wishes can come true!

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:07.780
Let's keep running down
 the road we believe in!

00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:15.690
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:15.690 --> 00:23:21.750
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:29.010
Will I ever make it that far?

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:32.400
Yeah, I'm almost there.

00:23:32.400 --> 00:23:38.270
I already made it this far, after all.

00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:53.130
That tears it, Shigeru!
You're always so self-centered.

00:23:53.600 --> 00:23:56.200
You may not want to be apart
from Domyoji...

00:23:56.430 --> 00:24:00.870
But to transfer to this school?!
What can you be thinking?!

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:05.910
Hana Yori Dango:
"The Shockwave of New Student Shigeru!"

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:09.040
Quit complicating my life!
